GL Code & Cost Code Prediction - Technical Documentation
Use Case: Machine Learning-Based GL Code and Cost Code Prediction for Non-PO Invoice Lines

1. Executive Summary
1.1 Business Problem
In accounts payable operations, invoices without Purchase Orders (Non-PO invoices) require manual assignment of General Ledger (GL) Codes and Cost Codes before approval. This manual process is:

Time-consuming: Approvers must research historical patterns to determine correct codes
Error-prone: Manual entry leads to inconsistent coding across similar invoices
Bottleneck-creating: Delays in code assignment slow down the approval workflow
Knowledge-dependent: Relies heavily on experienced approvers who understand vendor-code relationships
1.2 Solution Overview
The GL/CC Prediction System is an ML-powered Azure Function that automatically predicts GL Codes and Cost Codes for invoice line items using historical invoice data and ensemble machine learning techniques.

Technique	Purpose
Historical Pattern Learning	Trains on past invoice-to-code mappings
Two-Scope Architecture	Scope1 for exact matches, Scope2 for ML prediction
AdaBoost Classifier	Ensemble learning for high-accuracy predictions
Confidence Scoring	Provides prediction confidence for approver review
1.3 Key Capabilities
Automatic Training: Triggered when new training data is uploaded to blob storage
Two-Tier Prediction: Exact match lookup (Scope1) with ML fallback (Scope2)
Confidence Scores: Each prediction includes a confidence percentage
Dynamic Configuration: All field mappings and parameters are configurable via Azure Blob Storage
Multi-Format Support: Accepts CSV training file
Label Encoding: Automatic handling of categorical variables
Correlation Filtering: Removes highly correlated features to improve model quality
