6. Model Training Details
6.1 Data Preprocessing
Null Handling: Rows with any null values are dropped. Process fails if more than (100 - non_empty_value_percent)% data is dropped.

Numeric Cleaning: Numeric columns are cleaned for:

Comma separators (e.g., "1,234.56" → "1234.56")
Multiple decimal points (keeps last)
Type validation
Correlation Filtering: Columns with correlation > 0.85 are removed (keeps column with more unique values).

Single-Value Removal: Columns with only one unique value are dropped.

Label Encoding: All non-numeric columns are encoded using sklearn.LabelEncoder.

